];
---

<Article
  title="Pocket Option OTC: What It Is and How It Works"
  description="What OTC assets are on Pocket Option, why PocketOption OTC markets are open on weekends, and how their prices and payouts differ from regular market assets."
  h1="Pocket Option OTC assets explained"
  lead="What OTC means on Pocket Option, why it is open on weekends and how its payouts and prices differ from regular markets."
  crumb="Pocket Option OTC"
  parent={{ href: "/blog/", label: "Blog" }}
  toc={toc}
  article
  published="2026-11-19"
  updated="2026-11-19"
>
  <h2 id="what">What OTC means</h2>
  <p>
    OTC stands for over-the-counter. On Pocket Option, assets marked <strong>OTC</strong>, such as EUR/USD OTC, are
    priced by the broker and its liquidity providers rather than taken directly from an exchange or the interbank
    market.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because they do not depend on exchange hours, OTC assets stay open when regular markets are closed, including{" "}
    <strong>weekends and holidays</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="diff">OTC vs regular markets</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th></th>
        <th>Regular asset</th>
        <th>OTC asset</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Price source</td>
        <td>Market quotes</td>
        <td>Broker quotes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Hours</td>
        <td>Market hours</td>
        <td>24/7, including weekends</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>News impact</td>
        <td>Reacts to economic news</td>
        <td>May not follow real-world news</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Payout</td>
        <td>Varies</td>
        <td>Varies, check before each trade</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="tips">Trading OTC sensibly</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Do not assume an OTC chart will follow the real market. Analyse the OTC chart itself.</li>
    <li>Check the payout every time; it can change during the day.</li>
    <li>Use the same risk rules as on regular assets: small, fixed amounts.</li>
    <li>
      Test any weekend strategy on the <a href="/demo-account/">demo</a> first.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    For the basics of placing a trade, see <a href="/how-to-trade/">how to trade on Pocket Option</a>.
  </p>
</Article>
